1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,058
SAIIY: Good morning. Thanks for coming in to see us here at the agency, JOE.

2
00:00:06,058 --> 00:00:10,500
I'm one of the agency representatives, and my name's SALLY Baker.

3
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:13,600
JOE: Hi SALLY. I think we spoke on the phone, didn't we?

4
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:17,519
SALLY: That's right, we did. So thank you for sending in your CV.

5
00:00:17,519 --> 00:00:20,120
We've had quite a careful look at it

6
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:23,850
and I think we have two jobs that might be suitable for you.

7
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:25,150
JOE: OK.

8
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:28,160
SALLY: The first one is in a company based in North London

9
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:31,330
They're looking for an administrative assistant.

10
00:00:31,330 --> 00:00:34,450
JOE: OK. What sort of company is it?

11
00:00:34,450 --> 00:00:39,390
SALLY: They're called Home Solutions and they design and make furniture.

12
00:00:39,390 --> 00:00:43,680
JOE: Oh, I don't know much about that, but it sounds interesting.

13
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:47,299
SALLY: Yes, well as I said, they want someone in their office,

14
00:00:47,299 --> 00:00:50,380
and looking at your past experience it does look as

15
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:53,030
if you fit quite a few of the requirements.

16
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:57,250
So on your CV it appears you've done some data entry?

17
00:00:57,250 --> 00:00:58,450
JOE: Yes.

18
00:00:58,450 --> 00:01:00,717
SALLY: So that's one skill they want.

19
00:01:00,717 --> 00:01:05,250
Then they expect the person they appoint to attend meetings and take notes there...

20
00:01:05,250 --> 00:01:07,990
JOE: OK. I've done that before, yes.

21
00:01:07,990 --> 00:01:11,390
SALLY: And you'd need to be able to cope with general admin.

22
00:01:11,390 --> 00:01:13,943
JOE: Filing, and keeping records and so on?

23
00:01:13,943 --> 00:01:19,050
That should be OK. And in my last job I also had to manage the diary.

24
00:01:19,050 --> 00:01:21,763
SALLY: Excellent. That's something they want here too.

25
00:01:21,763 --> 00:01:27,190
I'd suggest you add it to your CV - I don't think you mentioned that, did you?

26
00:01:27,190 --> 00:01:28,190
JOE: No.

27
00:01:28,190 --> 00:01:31,702
SALLY: So as far as the requirements go,

28
00:01:31,702 --> 00:01:33,400
they want good computer skills, of course

29
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:36,970
and they particularly mention spreadsheets.

30
00:01:36,970 --> 00:01:38,350
JOE: That should be fine.

31
00:01:38,350 --> 00:01:42,960
SALLY: And interpersonal skills - which would be something they'd check with your references.

32
00:01:42,960 --> 00:01:45,810
JOE: I think that should be OK, yes.

33
00:01:45,810 --> 00:01:48,280
SALLY: Then they mention that they want someone

34
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:51,446
who is careful and takes care with details -

35
00:01:51,446 --> 00:01:55,320
just looking at your CV, I'd say you're probably alright there.

36
00:01:55,320 --> 00:02:00,210
JOE: I think so, yes. Do they want any special experience?

37
00:02:00,210 --> 00:02:03,850
SALLY: I think they wanted some experience of teleconferencing.

38
00:02:03,850 --> 00:02:06,950
JOE: I've got three years' experience of that.

39
00:02:06,950 --> 00:02:13,305
SALLY: Let's see, yes, good. In fact they're only asking for at least one year, so that's great.

40
00:02:13,305 --> 00:02:16,130
So is that something that might interest you?

41
00:02:16,130 --> 00:02:18,869
JOE: It is, yes. The only thing is,

42
00:02:18,869 --> 00:02:24,690
you said they were in North London so it would be quite a long commute for me.

43
00:02:24,690 --> 00:02:28,210
SALLY: OK.

44
00:02:28,210 --> 00:02:32,914
SALLY: So the second position might suit you better as far as the location goes;

45
00:02:32,914 --> 00:02:36,050
that's for a warehouse assistant and that's in South London.

46
00:02:36,050 --> 00:02:38,760
JOE: Yes, that would be a lot closer.

47
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:41,140
SALLY: And you've worked in a warehouse before, haven't you?

48
00:02:41,140 --> 00:02:42,240
JOE: Yes.

49
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:46,248
SALLY: So as far as the responsibilities for this position go,

50
00:02:46,248 --> 00:02:50,620
they want someone who can manage the stock, obviously, and also deliveries.

51
00:02:50,620 --> 00:02:55,020
JOE: That should be OK. You've got to keep track of stuff

52
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:57,970
but I've always been quite good with numbers.

53
00:02:57,970 --> 00:03:00,147
SALLY: Good. that's their first requirement.

54
00:03:00,147 --> 00:03:04,500
And they want someone who's computer literate, which we know you are.

55
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:06,340
JOE: Sure.

56
00:03:06,340 --> 00:03:08,800
SALLY: Then they mention organisational skills

57
00:03:09,140 --> 00:03:11,410
They want someone who's well organised.

58
00:03:11,410 --> 00:03:14,100
JOE: Yes, I think I am.

59
00:03:14,100 --> 00:03:15,630
SALLY: And tidy?

60
00:03:15,630 --> 00:03:18,800
JOE: Yes, they go together really, don't they?

61
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:21,140
SALLY: Sure. Then the usual stuff

62
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:25,620
they want someone who can communicate well both orally and in writing.

63
00:03:25,620 --> 00:03:29,080
JOE: OK. And for the last warehouse job I had

64
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:33,470
one of the things I enjoyed most was being part of a team.

65
00:03:33,470 --> 00:03:36,150
I found that was really essential for the job.

66
00:03:36,150 --> 00:03:41,309
SALLY: Excellent. Yes, they do mention that they want someone who's used to that, yes.

67
00:03:41,309 --> 00:03:44,960
Now when you were working in a warehouse last time

68
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:47,500
what sorts of items were you dealing with?

69
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:54,280
JOE: It was mostly bathroom and kitchen equipment, sinks and stoves and fridges.

70
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:57,570
SALLY: So you're OK moving heavy things?

71
00:03:57,570 --> 00:04:01,350
JOE: Sure. I'm quite strong, and I've had the training.

72
00:04:01,350 --> 00:04:05,020
SALLY: Good. Now as far as experience goes

73
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:06,854
they mention they want someone with a licence,

74
00:04:06,854 --> 00:04:11,000
and that you have experience of driving in London

75
00:04:11,020 --> 00:04:13,390
so you can cope with the traffic and so on.

76
00:04:13,390 --> 00:04:15,440
JOE: Yes, no problem.

77
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:18,080
SALLY: And you've got experience of warehouse work

78
00:04:18,580 --> 00:04:21,364
and the final thing they mention is customer service.

79
00:04:21,364 --> 00:04:24,500
I think looking at your CV you're OK there.

80
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:28,850
JOE: Right. So what about pay? Can you tell me a bit more about that, please...
